 so that's kind of another place where  this dilemma kind of takes place because  jesse's like well we have to keep you  safe but he's like but i'm not living  you know what i mean so it's that even  though a lot of that is unspoken that's  uh clearly what the conflict is that's  going on  so at some point uh thomas does try to  contact like an outsider like a neighbor  kid and stuff like that and you know  that  that isn't the one thing that like sets  off this series of events but there is  one particular thing or actually it's  not even one particular thing but there  is kind of like a breaking down of the  routine which leads from one event to  another which just makes this situation  more and more untenable like as the  movie goes on uh as i said i'm not going  to spoil the ending because it's a  fairly new movie and it hasn't been on  the streaming services for all that long  but as i said don't go into this  expecting it is a vampire movie  but don't go into it expecting like you  know blade or dracula like you know  anything like a classical traditional  vampire type of story this is much more  like  using vampirism as sort of like a  metaphorical thing to explore  the sacrifices that family members make  the things that they have to do to like  keep their loved ones alive even if  those things are really really in this  case uh really really terrible and  really really evil and like how far  would you go  um if you had a loved one that had that  needed this and would you end up doing  what these siblings did for their  brother so as i said if you like stuff  like this thematically this is similar  to let the right one end it's like a  totally different vibe to that movie  like don't think that it's similar but  thematically it's kind of like explore  some of the same  themes as let the right one in as i said  uh the addiction martin movies like that  if you like vampire movies that are more  like that then you'll probably dig this  one as well um i actually quite liked it  it is quite slow uh it is very bleak it  is very grim  but you guys know i kind of like that  kind of thing so if you like that kind  of thing then this is very easy to watch  i believe it's streaming for free on 2b  it's also on shutter as of this  recording and i'm pretty sure it's also  on amazon prime as well so if that  sounds interesting at all to you then  please check it out and if you've seen  it uh let me know what you thought about  it in the comments and that will do it  for this uh installment of flickers of  fear and i will see you guys on the next  one bye
 

